med or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are eight containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is an unoriented  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm lumpectomy specimen with a needle localization wire running through the center of the specimen along the 3 9cm axis  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm tan  firm  ovoid mass with a flat  cut edge protrudes through one aspect of the specimen  and is 1 2cm from one long axis end margin and 2 6cm from the other long axis margin  The remainder of the specimen surface is adipose  fragmented  but otherwise grossly unremarkable  The external surface of the specimen is inked black  the firm mass is now removed  and the area underlying it is inked blue  The specimen is serially sectioned along the long axis to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm area consisting of multiple well circumscribed soft  friable tan nodules  of which the largest is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The clip is identified within the largest nodule  This area abuts the black inked margin approximately 0 4cm from the previously described firm mass  and is 0 2cm from the firm mass  and is 0 7cm from the opposing black inked margin  The area is 1 6cm from one end margin  and 1 8cm from the other end margin  Leading towards the soft mass and abutting it is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fibrous area consistent with biopsy tract  The remaining breast parenchyma is fibroadipose  and grossly unremarkable  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   End margin closest to mass  en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Soft nodules to closest black inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Soft nodules to opposite margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Largest nodule to closest black inked margin in area of firm mass  with the portion of specimen where the firm mass was removed overinked blue   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Further representative sections of soft nodular area   REM