urface is inked yellow  The specimen is sectioned vertically from right to left to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm biopsy cavity with a wall that is tan to tan pink  focally granular  coming focally within 0 1cm of the inked resection margin  Granular tissue from the biopsy cavity wall abuts the resection margin in a number of locations  Over 95  of the specimen is submitted from medial to lateral as A through Z as follows  A  medial end  en face  red ink indicates inferior portion  B D F H J L N P R T V X  superior  from medial to lateral  C E G I K M O Q S U W Y  inferior  from medial to lateral  Z  lateral margin  en face  Designated  Left axillary node tissue   is a 40 gm  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 3cm in maximum dimension axillary lymph node dissection  Nodes are submitted as AA through EE  Designated  Additional axillary tissue   is a 0 3cm in diameter node and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm piece of fatty tissue  submitted in toto as FF  In addition there is a 0 2cm tan to fatty piece of tissue  submitted in toto as GG  Resident  James Kirby  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  L Celeste Robb Nicholson  M D  PART A  LYMPH NODE  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLARY TISSUE   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   LUMPECTOMY   report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 09 39 CLINICAL DATA  History of infiltrating ductal carcinoma of right breast in  REMOVED_CASE_ID                                                                                       FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  75    REMOVED_DATE CM  MULTIFOCAL  PRESENT ON 5 OF 6 SLIDES  EXTENDING TO ANTERIOR AND SUPERIOR MARGINS ALONG BROAD FRONTS  NEGATIVE FOR LYMPHOVASCULAR INVASION  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  25    PRESENT ON 3 OF 6 SLIDES  EXTENDING TO A SUPERIOR MARGIN  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 11 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 09     SPECIAL STAINS Addendum     NOTE  Because of impression of endocrine differentiation  an argyrophil stain is performed  but it is negative  Added by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 19 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm oriented fragment of fibroadipose tissue  with two long stitches indicating the lateral margin  a short and a long stitch indicating the anterior margin  and two short stitches indicating the superior margin  The posterior aspect of the specimen is inked black  the anterior aspect is inked blue  and the superior aspect is inked orange  The specimen is sectioned lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm ill defined  firm  tan white area with a central area of hemorrhage present 0 3cm from the deep  posterior  black  margin  0 7cm from the lateral margin  0 4cm from the anterior  blue  margin  and 0 8cm from the superior  orange  margin  The specimen is submitted entirely  lateral to medial  in A F  Gross Description by  RHONDA YANTISS  MD Resident  MELINDA J  FAN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   LEFT BREAST   SMALL WELL DEFINED LESION  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  ESTHER OLIVA  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
