oratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 AUG 98 at 14 15     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     The anterior resection margin of the specimen is focally positive at REMOVED_DATE o clock  Added by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  14 AUG 98 at 18 17 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm mastectomy specimen  with an overlying REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm circular portion of white skin  with a central  grossly unremarkable nipple areolar complex  There is no grossly visible scar  There is a suture on one aspect of the skin designating the 12 o clock margin  The entire specimen is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a central  irregular  focally gritty area  possibly consistent with a previous biopsy site  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  This area is located 2 0cm beneath the overlying skin and comes within 3 5cm of the closest deep margin  and 1 5cm of the closest anterior margin  at REMOVED_DATE o clock   This possible biopsy site  in relation to the closest anterior margin at REMOVED_DATE o clock is submitted in Cassettes A B  The remainder of the biopsy cavity is submitted in Cassette C  Representative sections of this region in relation to the overlying skin are submitted in Cassettes D E  Further section of the medial half of the specimen reveals focal areas of fibrosis with minimal gritty areas  which come within 1 0cm and 2 5cm of the closest REMOVED_DATE o clock anterior margin  Representative sections of these areas are submitted in Cassettes F H  Further sectioning reveals a dense area of fibrosis centrally located  from which multiple blue domed cysts are identified  A representative section from the lateral aspect at the 11 o clock position is submitted in Cassette I  In the lateral aspect  at the 6 o clock position inferiorly  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm pink  healed  retracted area possibly consistent with a previous biopsy site  which comes within 2 5cm from the closest anterior margin and 3 5cm from the closest deep margin  The area is submitted in toto in Cassette J  On a line parallel to the 6 and 12 o clock margins  there is a gritty  focally cystic REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm area  which comes within 0 7cm of the deep margin  This area is submitted entirely in Cassette K  The remaining fibrous areas are focally cystic  No additional abnormalities are noted  No lymph nodes are noted in the most lateral aspect  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast axillary contents   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm portion of adipose tissue  from which multiple lymph nodes are identified  ranging from   0 1cm in greatest dimension  up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  A representative section from each lymph is submitted in Cassettes L O  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  SELIM NASSER  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  Edi Brogi  M D   PhD  PART A  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION   report_end  , Unchecked.
