Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13 57 CLINICAL DATA  A core biopsy of a mammographic lesion revealed infiltrating ductal carcinoma and ductal carcinoma in situ                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 3 OF 3  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE TO HIGH GRADE  PRESENT ON 8 0F 14 SLIDES  EXTENDING FAR AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF SEVERAL INKED MARGINS  SEE NOTE  3  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  4  FAT NECROSIS CONSISTENT WITH HEALING CORE BIOPSY SITE  NOTE  The examined margins are free of invasive tumor  but carcinoma in situ is quite close to margins on several slides  and is distributed throughout several sections that contain no invasive tumor  Minor areas resembling lobular carcinoma in situ are interpreted as cancerization of lobules by intraductal carcinoma  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION OF ADDITIONAL INFERIOR MARGIN  1  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  TWO FOCI AT CAUTERIZED INKED MARGINS  SLIDE Z   2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  3  FAT NECROSIS  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLARY   HOTSPOT    BIOPSY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  ONE LYMPH NODE   LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  LEVEL I   REGIONAL DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 10 OF 10 LYMPH NODES  SUBMITTED AS LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLARY  LEVEL II   REGIONAL DISSECTION  ADIPOSE TISSUE ONLY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 23 32                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 11 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue oriented with a short suture indicating superior margin and a long suture designating lateral margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an irregular shaped  white  firm mass abutting the inferior margin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The specimen is entirely submitted from lateral to medial with one half of the first section in A  the other half in B  etc  through cassette N  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right axilla hotspot  1  CT  811  is a 2 x 