Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 58 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3   EXTENDING TO THE SURGICAL MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  Note  The tumor mass is 2cm in greatest dimension  Histologically  multiple geographically separate foci of infiltrating tumor are present  The tumor is almost entirely infiltrating  with only a small focus of in situ carcinoma  The infiltrating component has a predominantly alveolar pattern  Lymphatic invasion is present  The alveolar pattern raises the possibility of neuroendocrine differentiation  Positivity of the tumor cells for synaptophysin by immunoperoxidase lends some support to this  However  the tumor is negative for chromogranin  and a Grimelius stain is negative  Diagnosis by  Daniel Rubin  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 01                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 243 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Positive 61 fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 34     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  EXCISION   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   3   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization o