Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 11 10 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  MEASURED FROM SLIDES   GRADE 1 OF 3  REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE CLOSEST MARGIN  WITHOUT FOR LYMPHATIC OR BLOOD VASCULAR INVASION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  CRIBRIFORM AND SOLID TYPE WITH FOCAL NECROSIS  INVOLVING MANY DUCTS THROUGHOUT THE SPECIMEN  AND PRESENT AT SEVERAL MARGINS  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 19 24                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm portion of fibroadipose tissue which is oriented with two short sutures where the superior aspect  two long sutures for the medial  and one long and one short for anterior  There is a needle localization wire and accompanying specimen radiograph  The entire specimen is inked black while the anterior surface is double inked yellow  medial blue  and posterior green  The specimen is sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a 0 3cm in diameter firm gray stellate area  too small to freeze  The specimen is submitted in its entirety from superior to inferior in cassettes A through F  with the lesion in cassette B   D  Gross Description by  JANINE L  DUDAC Resident  ERIN OCHOA  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST MASS  SUSPICIOUS LESION    CARCINOMA    RADIAL SCAR  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  JAMES J  TIESINGA  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Lawrence R  Zukerberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Unchecked.
