                                            IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block P   The tumor cells stain faintly for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  14 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 15 49     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Left  block P   HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 10 55 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast tissue lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 7cm irregular  tan yellow to pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue with a long suture designating the lateral aspect and short suture designating the superior aspect  The specimen contains three localizing needle wires  The posterior aspect is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  The specimen is sequentially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm well circumscribed dark red hemorrhagic cavity  located 1 0cm from the lateral  1 3cm from the posterior  1 5cm from the anterior  2 4cm from the inferior  and 4 5cm from the superior margins  The cavity is filled with dark red clotted blood and the walls are slightly indurated and contain a metal clip  The surrounding area is tan yellow to white  rubbery and lobulated  There are numerous cystic nodular areas containing thick tan white pasty material diffusely located throughout this area  This abuts the anterior  posterior and superior margins  comes to 0 5cm from the inferior  0 8cm from the lateral  and 1 0cm from the medial margins  There is a minimum amount of uninvolved tissue consisting of tan yellow to pink unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Medial margin  radially sectioned   B C  Hemorrhagic cavity with anterior and posterior margins  D  Inferior margin  E  Anterior and posterior margins  F  Superior and posterior margins  G  Lateral margin  radially sectioned   P U  Additional sections of parenchyma  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  sentinel node hot and blue left axilla  REMOVED_CASE_ID   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan pink lymph node with a moderate amount of attached tan yellow lobulated adipose tissue  The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional superior nodule  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm unoriented irregular tan yellow to pink rubbery nodule  The specimen is inked black  serially sectioned to reveal a tan yellow homogeneous rubbery cut surface with multiple tan yellow well delineated nodules averaging 0 1cm in diameter and extending to the closest margin of the resection  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassette I  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional media