Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Massachusetts General Hospital  Boston  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Tel  617  REMOVED_DATE    Surgical Pathology Report      Accession     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  E   DOB  REMOVED_DATE  Age  37   Sex  F  MRN   REMOVED_CASE_ID   Location  Same Day Surgery Unit  Institution  MGH  Date of Operation  REMOVED_DATE  Date of Accession  REMOVED_DATE  Reported  REMOVED_DATE 12 55  Results To   Michelle Connolly Specht MD      FINAL PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS   A  BREAST EXCISION  LEFT   No residual carcinoma   See note    Healing biopsy site with clip     Note  Per medical records  this patient received neoadjuvant chemotherapy for  primary breast cancer  There is no residual in situ or invasive carcinoma  identified in this excision specimen  The clip site was submitted for  histologic evaluation and the surrounding fibrous tissue was generously sampled   Definite treatment effect is not identified  scattered aggregates of  macrophages  some hemosiderin laden  could represent treatment effect  but could  also be related to the prior biopsy procedure     The pathology findings represent a complete pathologic response  and would  correspond to Miller Payne grade 5  of 5  and Residual Cancer Burden of 0       B  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT SUPERIOR   There is no evidence of malignancy       C  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT INFERIOR   There is no evidence of malignancy       D  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT MEDIAL   There is no evidence of malignancy       E  BREAST EXCISION FINAL MARGIN  LEFT LATERAL   There is no evidence of malignancy         Note  The resection margins of the specimen s  were inked and microscopically  evaluated  see individual gross descriptions     This case does not contain all the coding components for CMS PQRI measure  99        Electronically Signed Out By Amy Ly MD       Resident Pathologist   Sa