ree  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are four containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  right axilla sentinel node hot and blue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm tan pink to yellow nodular soft tissue  bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1  now resubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled  sentinel node left axilla 491   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm fatty soft tissue consistent with lymph node  bisected and entirely frozen as FX 2 and FX 2A  now resubmitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   respectively  Received fresh  labeled  simple mastectomy short stitch   superior  long stitch   lateral  left    is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm left simple mastectomy with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm tan skin ellipse contains a 3 0cm in diameter nipple areolar complex  The overlying skin and nipple areolar complex are grossly unremarkable  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma  No axillary lymph nodes are identified  Representative sections are submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  right simple mastectomy  short   superior  long   lateral   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm right simple mastectomy specimen with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral  The overlying REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm tan skin ellipse contains a 3 0cm nipple areolar complex  which is grossly unremarkable  There is a 4 0cm curvilinear  well healed scar superior and lateral to the nipple  The specimen is inked as follows  Anterior   blue  posterior   black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined  tan  stellate  firm lesion in the mid portion of the breast  consistent with prior biopsy site  The breast tissue just lateral to this region is stained blue green  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Biopsy cavity to closest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Remaining biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections away from biopsy cavity  INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS  FROZEN SECTION  1  SENTINEL NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  2A  SENTINEL NODE  LEFT AXILLA   NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON    1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The ductal carcinoma in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Estrogen and progesterone receptor quantitation  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells is assessed visually and reported as follows  The tumor cells stain    10  of nuclei stained  Some tumor cells stain  1 to  10  of nuclei stained  Rare tumor cells stain    1  of nuclei stained  The tumor cells do not stain  0  of nuclei stained  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 