CESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The rest of the soft tissue is submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin and labeled  sentinel node  705  left axilla   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm fibrofatty soft tissue containing a candidate lymph node  which is bisected and entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin and labeled  sentinel node  135  left axilla   is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm fibrofatty soft tissue containing a lymph node  The lymph node is trisected and submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The rest of the soft tissue is submitted entirely in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin and labeled  sentinel node  256  left axilla   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fibrofatty soft tissue and lymph node  entirely submitted in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   bisected  Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 05   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 03 24 52PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON   1 QUANTITATIVE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erbB 2 Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  HER 2 c erbB 2 quantitation  the tumor cells membrane immunoreactivity is evaluated visually and reported as follows  Do not show overexpression  0 to 1   no minimal immunoreactivity or incomplete membrane staining of tumor cells  Show moderate  2   overexpression  weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  Show strong  3   overexpression  strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in   10  of tumor cells  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum  1 by Atul K Bhan M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 10   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 09 08 25AM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left   Excision PART B  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   Sentinel   723   Excision PART C  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   Sentinel  705   Excision PART D  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   Sentinel  135   Excision PART E  Lymph Node  Left Axilla   Sentinel  256   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 54 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST MASS  LEFT   WIDE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  AS MEASURED FROM A GLASS SLIDE  WITH CENTRAL HYALINIZING FIBROSIS AND NECROSIS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE WITHIN AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS  LYMPH NODES   LEFT AXILLA  DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 15 OUT OF 15 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY LEFT   TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 6 OUT OF 6 LYMPH NODES  BREAST  ADDITIONAL DEEP   RE EXCISION  BREAST TISSUE WITH STROMAL FIBROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR TO DEEP MARGIN   CAUTERIZED BREAST TISSUE WITH INVOLUTIONAL CHANGE AND FOCAL MICROCALIFICATIONS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  No definite lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is seen  although several suspicious foci are identified  The examined margin of resection appears free of carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See Note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in multiple parts  Labeled  wide excision  left breast  and received fresh from the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  There is a short stitch and a long stitch designating the superior and the lateral margins resectively  The superior margin is inked in green and lateral in red  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm  ill defined nodule  present at 0 2cm from the closest inferior margin  A representative section of the nodule and inferior margin is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in cassette A  B to D are tumor with additional inferior margins  E to H are sections of superior margin  I and J are sections of the lateral and medial margins submitted en face  Labeled  left axillary contents  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fatty tissue are multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in maximum dimension and disected from this fatty tissue which is submitted in cassettes K V  Cassettes M V contain half of each lymph node  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of fatty tissue  Six lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm and disected from this fatty tissue  The lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes Q and R  Labeled  additional  superior and deep margin excision  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  No mass is identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes S T and U  Labeled  additional  inferior to deep margin  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  No lesion is identified  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes V and W  Resident  Navneet Narula  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECITON DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRAITING CARCINOMA  MARGINS FREE OF TUMOR  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST MASS  LEFT   WIDE EXCISION PART B  AXILLARY  LEFT   CONTENTS PART C  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY  LEFT   TISSUE PART D  ADDITIONAL DEEP  RE EXCISION PART E  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR TO DEEP MARGIN   report_end  , Unchecked.
