Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  22 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 46 CLINICAL DATA  Prior lumpectomy and radiation therapy 16 years ago  now with a new lump in a separate quadrant  which was found to be cancerous by core biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE 2 OF 3  SEE NOTE  2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  SEVERAL DUCTS WITHIN THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  Note  The resection margins are free of tumor  No lymphotic or vascular invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 28 Proofread by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of