Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  12 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 13 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  3 CM  MODERATELY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE II III  FOCALLY PRESENT AT THE ANTERIOR SOFT TISSUE RESECTION MARGIN  WITH LYMPHATIC INVASION   SEE NOTE   MULTIPLE LEVELS EXAMINED  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE CARCINOMA  EXTENDING TO WITHIN 1 MM OF THE DEEP  POSTERIOR  RESECTION MARGIN  HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  NOTE  No definitive blood vessel invasion is seen  Diagnosis by  Jacqueline Haas  MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 13 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 16 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm fragment of fibrofatty tissue with a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm skin ellipse  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 4cm stellate  firm  tan white mass with gritty cut surface  extending to 0 9cm from the deep margin  and less than 0 5cm from the closest anterior soft tissue resection margin  adjacent to the skin   No frozen section is done  SECTION CODE A  Tumor and closest posterior soft tissue resection margin  B  Tumor and closest anterior soft tissue resection margin  contiguous section with that in A   C  Additional sections of tumor and anterior soft tissue resection margin  D  Additional representative section of the tumor and adjacent posterior soft tissue resection margin  contiguous to the section in C   E  Additional representative section of the tumor adjacent to the anterior margin  F  Additional representative section of the posterior soft tissue resection margin and along the lateral soft tissue resection margin  overinked yellow   Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS   RIGHT BREAST   HIGHLY SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA  NO FROZEN SECTION DONE  O R  Resident  RHONDA YANTISS  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  David L Berger  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT  EXCISION , Unchecked.
