Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  20 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 17 54 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  95   REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  PRESENT AT MULTIPLE INKED RESECTION MARGINS  WITH FOCAL DUCTAL PAGETOID SPREAD  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Infiltrating carcinoma is present in all sections and involves approximately 60  of the specimen  No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  5   DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  CRIBRIFORM TYPE  SMALL MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  NOTE  DR  FRITZ KOERNER CONCURS WITH THIS INTERPRETATION FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  Diagnosis by  G  Richard Dickersin  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 44                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  A few tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 52 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 8cm mass of hard fibrofatty tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a hard gritty irregular mass that replaces approximately 35  of the total area of the specimen and extends to several inked margins  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and saved frozen  Representative sections of the remainder in A through J  Resident  Joseph Misdraji  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
