g Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 MAY 00 at 07 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  sentinel node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fibrofatty fragment of tissue  entirely frozen as FX 1  resubmitted as A  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  short superior  long lateral  left breast  is a left mastectomy measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 4cm  with an overlying skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm  including the nipple  The skin ellipse harbors a short superior stitch and a long lateral stitch  The specimen is inked and sagitally sectioned through its posterior aspect  On sectioning the breast parenchyma shows multiple areas of vaguely nodular dense white rubbery tissue  with lobulated contours  In one area  the parenchyma is firmer and has more stellate configuration  This abnormal area averaging REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm lies within an area of bland looking tissue  It is located 1 3cm from the deep margin  in the lateral aspect of the breast  3 5cm from the nipple  Part of the lesion is sampled for the tumor bank  Sections are submitted as follows  B C  Tumor  relation to deep margin  D E  Additional sections from tumor  F G  Distant breast parenchyma  medial side  H  Two lymph nodes  isolated from short axillary tail attached to the mastectomy  Submitted entire  Resident  LAURENCE DE LEVAL  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     LYMPH NODE  LEFT SENTINEL   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  AARON CAPLAN  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO