Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 2 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Signed Out by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Cancer of the left breast FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  CHANGES CONSISTENT WITH CHEMOTHERAPY  NO RESIDUAL CARCINOMA IDENTIFIED  HYALINIZED FIBROADENOMA  LYMPH NODES  LEFT AXILLA   MASTECTOMY  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 3 OF 3 LYMPH NODES  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received unfixed  labeled  Rose Mbanya  REMOVED_DATE  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm modified radical mastectomy with attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm axillary tissue containing a black suture  The specimen is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 16 0cm tan brown skin ellipse bearing an unremarkable nipple and a 2 5cm healed linear scar along the inferomedial aspect of the areola  The anterior margin is inked black  and the posterior is inked black  The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm poorly delineated fibrous area with edematous change and chalky yellow foci  This region corresponds to the scar on the skin surface and extends to 4 5cm from the posterior margin  A silver metal clip lies in the lower outer quadrant which is located 8 5cm lateral to the aforementioned area  Near the clip is a vague REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm gray white stellate fibrous area  which extends to 8 0cm from the posterior margin  Finally there is a well defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm gray pink homogeneous rubbery nodule in the mid superior breast tissue  which extends