Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  AMY S  COLWELL  M D  Resident  Elizabeth Demicco  M D   Ph D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 49 year old woman with a history of left breast cancer undergoing re excision  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  MINUTE FOCUS OF RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  2  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  5  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  6  SKIN WITH SCAR WITH FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  SEE TABLE 1 AND NOTE  B  BREAST  LEFT ADDITIONAL INFERIOR   EXCISION  1  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA TUMOR SIZE   0 1cm  microscopic measurement  see note  GRADE  2  LYMPHATIC VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  BLOOD VESSEL INVASION  Not identified  MARGIN OF INVASIVE CARCINOMA  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  LOCATION OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  Within and beyond the region of the invasive carcinoma  GRADE OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2  MARGIN OF DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  The distances to all margins measure 0 2cm or greater  STAINS FOR RECEPTORS  See prior report MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   NOTE  Residual invasive carcinoma is present in a minute focus measuring less than 0 1cm  Extensive DCIS is present in 5 of 8 blocks in the multiple separate foci both in association with the healing biopsy site and in other areas of the breast  A panel of immunostains including p63  calponin  myosin and cytokeratin performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  confirm the presence of residual invasive carcinoma  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers which are  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh  labeled  left breast   is a 540 gram  REMOVED_DATE x 15 x 3 2cm left simple mastectomy specimen  On the anterior surface  there is a 9 x 4 5cm portion of skin  consisting of 6cm linear scar with up to 0 5cm of skin excised on either side of it  attached to a REMOVED_DATE x 3cm areolar complex  with 1 x 1 x 0 6cm nipple  The specimen is oriented with a stitch designating the axillary tail  Also received in the same container are 2 portions of skin aggregating to 8 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm  The anterior surface of the specimen is inked blue  and the posterior inked black  and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm ill defined firm mass with central fat necrosis and surgical clips  located in the upper outer quadrant of the breast towards the axillary tail  The mass approaches to 0 3cm of the posterior margin  and 2 5cm of the anterior margin  The remainder of the breast is primarily fibroadipose tissue  with small areas of fibrocystic change  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Mass to nearest posterior margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nearest anterior margin radially towards mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional sections through mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section of fibrocystic change adjacent to mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Sections of apparently unremarkable fibroadipose tissue distant from mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Section through scar on skin  and representative sections through also separately submitted skin in same container  Received in formalin  labeled  additional inferior tissue  left breast   are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue  aggregating to 5 x 4 x 0 8cm  The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 27   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 06 02 18PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART A  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Breast  Left Additional inferior   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 07  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  Christopher K Hysell  M D  Signed Out by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  CLINICAL DATA  64 year old female with invasive ductal carcinoma of the right breast FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  HEALING BIOPSY SITE SEE NOTE  NOTE  Stains for p63 protein  calponin  keratin  and myosin heavy chain do not disclose carcinoma  The lobular carcinoma cells do not stain for E cadherin  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received unfixed  labeled  Cynthia Norton  REMOVED_DATE  right breast  is a 910 gram simple mastectomy specimen  which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm and is surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 10 3cm ellipse of skin with an unremarkable nipple  The surgeon denotes the axillary tail with a suture  The anterior margin is inked blue  and the posterior margin is inked black  The specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cavity with variegated  yellow red and tan discoloration of the surrounding tissue  The cavity extends to 0 7cm from the anterior margin  3 5cm from the posterior margin  and greater than 5 0cm from the remaining margins  1 0cm lateral to the cavity there is a 0 7cm region of yellow red discoloration of the fat  1 0cm medial and 5 0cm superior  in the 12 o clock region  is a 0 4cm tan nodule  which is greater than 3 0cm from all margins  Lymph nodes are not identified in the axillary tail  The following cassettes are submitted  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative posterior margin  underlying the cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavity with relationship to anterior margin in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Tissue lateral to the biopsy cavity such that this discoloration is entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule in the 12 o clock region such that it is entirely submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of unremarkable breast parenchyma away from cavity from the medial aspect of the specimen with posterior margin included   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of unremarkable breast parenchyma away from the cavity from the lateral aspect of the specimen with posterior margin included  Fellow Review by Christopher K Hysell M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  Same Day Surgery  WACC 3 Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 3 Results To  KEVIN S  HUGHES  M D  Signed Out by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  CLINICAL DATA  Carcinoma in the right breast FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU SCATTERED MICROSCOPIC FOCI SHOWING TWO MORPHOLOGICAL PATTERNS  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU   AMPUTATION NEUROMA  HEALING SURGICAL SITE  SEE NOTE  SEE TABLE  1  NOTE  Stains for cytokeratin REMOVED_DATE  cytokeratin 14  and E cadherin were evaluated  TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS  1 DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Tumor Size  Scattered microscopic foci involving 7 of 20 blocks  Grade  1  major population  and 2  minor population  Margin of Ductal Carcinoma In Situ  Ductal carcinoma in situ extends to less than 0 1cm from the inferior margin of the specimen in one focus and to 0 1cm from the superior margin of the specimen in one focus  Stains for Receptors  Not indicated  see specimen number MS 09  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   GROSS DESCRIPTION  In fixative  labeled  Janice Alden  REMOVED_DATE  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 2cm piece of fibroadipose tissue with a short suture designating the superior aspect  a long suture designating the lateral aspect  and a bowtie suture designating the cephalad aspect  The anterior margin of the specimen is inked blue  the posterior black  the superior green  and the inferior yellow  The specimen consists of lobulated tan yellow fat and interspersed dense  gray white nodular fibrous tissue  which extends to the medial  lateral  anterior  and posterior margins and to 1 5cm from the superior margin and 1 8cm from the inferior margin  The tissue adjacent to the fibrous tissue shows chalky  yellow white discoloration and contains metal clips  A metal clip is evident at the posterior aspect of the specimen  The following sections are submitted   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial end en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Lateral end en face   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous tissue from medial to lateral   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Additional tissue Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on Tuesday May 12   REMOVED_CASE_ID  at 12 15 24PM By his her signature above  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  PART   Breast  Right   Excision  report_end  , Unchecked.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 43 CLINICAL DATA  48 year old female post menopausal who had a palpable breast mass in REMOVED_MONTH at which time she was on Premarin  No palpable lymphadenopathy  On exam  solid lesion at 10 o clock lateral to areola  on ultrasound solid lesion  Now for excisional biopsy of right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISION   INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  80     MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3    DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  20      SEE NOTE   NOTE  The infiltrating carcinoma measures 1 8cm in greatest dimension and is present at several surgical resection margins  ER and PR receptor studies will be reported in an addendum  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  The gross frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Michael Pins  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 08 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right breast mass  is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm tan red  yellow fragment of fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal one small focus of borderline suspicion that is too small for frozen section analysis  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes A through D  Resident  Ross C  Wheeler  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  Martha Elizabeth Meaney  M D  PART   BREAST MASS  RIGHT    report_end  , Unchecked.
