Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  08 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 15 CLINICAL DATA  Breast mass with atypical cytology on fine needle aspiration                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY    INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  95    REMOVED_DATE CM BY GROSS MEASUREMENT  GRADE 2 OF 3  EXTENDING TO MULTIPLE MARGINS  SEE NOTE    DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  5    ASSOCIATED WITH AND ADJACENT TO THE INVASIVE COMPONENT    SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  NOTE  No lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is identified  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 42                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast mass   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of breast  which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm hard ill defined tan mass abutting numerous inked margins  Representative tumor sections are submitted in A through D  representative fibrous tissue in E and F  A representative section is frozen as frozen section  1  and submitted in G  Resident  GARY LETTS  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  MARISA BALDASSANO  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  GARY LETTS  M D  PART   BREAST MASS  LEFT    report_end  , Unchecked.
