ng axis  The cut surface of the first fragment has a smooth homogeneous yellow white appearance and is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The cut surface of the second fragment has a smooth homogenous yellow white appearance with focal red grey areas within 0 5cm from one end  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  red grey areas   The third fragment has a uniform pink yellow appearance on its cut surface and is submitted entirely in cassettes  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Rosalynn M Nazarian M D   on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Rosalynn M Nazarian M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Review by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Frederick Carl Koerner M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Less than 10  of the in situ tumor cells stain faintly for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain faintly for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  1 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE ADDENDUM NOTE  REASON  RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS  Please see Addendum  1  Addendum by Elena F Brachtel M D   on REMOVED_DATE Addendum  2 by Elena F Brachtel M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART   BREAST  LEFT   EXCISION , Checked.
