om the overlying scar  and a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm indurated  tan white  stellate area along the inferior aspect which comes to within  0 1cm from the inferior blue inked anterior soft tissue margin  5 0cm from the black inked posterior aspect and 3 0cm from the overlying skin  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is tan yellow to pink unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  Within the attached axillary tail a few possible tan pink lymph nodes are ranging from 0 3cm to 1 2cm in maximum dimension  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Representative sections of posterior deep margin taken en face directly overlying suspicious area  B D  Representative sections of overlying skin containing dimpling effect  E H  Indurated stellate area  entirely submitted  with the closest inferior blue inked anterior soft tissue margin in cassette E  I J  Fibrous tract to overlying scar and surrounding tissue  K L  Uninvolved fibrous tissue  M  Three whole possible lymph nodes  N  One possible lymph node  O  One possible lymph node  P  One bisected lymph node  R  Four whole possible lymph nodes  S  Four whole possible lymph nodes  T  Five whole possible lymph nodes  U  Four whole possible lymph nodes  R U  Additional lymph nodes  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional left axillary tissue  are REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm of irregular tan yellow to pink fibroadipose tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm tan pink lymph nodes  The specimen is submitted in toto in cassette Q  Gross Description by  JENNIFER NASH Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  SGR                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST LEFT AXILLA ADDITIONAL  EXCISION , Unchecked.
