 receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  07 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 59 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast   is a 670 gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm modified radical mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm overlying skin ellipse containing an unremarkable nipple and a 3 0cm long circum areolar healed surgical incision 2 0cm inferomedial to the nipple  The resection margins are inked and the specimen is serially sectioned from the posterior surface to reveal a hard  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm  irregular  white  fibrotic area with a central yellowish region identified directly deep to the circum areolar healed incision  this is presumed to be the biopsy cavity and it is 1 5cm from the deep margin  The rest of the breast parenchyma shows multiple ill defined areas of tan white  fibrotic tissue scattered throughout the breast  The axillary tail is separated from the main mass and sampled for lymph nodes  which measure in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm in aggregate  SECTION CODE  A  nipple  B  healed incision  C D  presumed biopsy cavity  E  deep margin  F H  representative sections of breast tissue  I J  representative sections of suspicious area adjacent to axillary tail  K  lymph nodes  Labeled  Left breast  additional axillary tissue   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of yellow tan  soft tissue  submitted entirely in L  Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  F